{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"blockCutTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity12BlockCutTreeV","text":"BlockCutTree","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BlockCutTree"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/blockcuttree()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/blockCutTree()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Inherited from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph.blockCutTree()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P12ConnectivityE12blockCutTreeAD05BlockeF0VyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV","title":"blockCutTree()","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/UndirectedConnectivity.swift#L113","fileName":"UndirectedConnectivity.swift"},"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"blockCutTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BlockCutTree","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity12BlockCutTreeV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"references":{"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"Hypergraphs","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs","identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView/blockCutTree()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/blockCutTree()","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview\/blockcuttree()","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"blockCutTree()","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"blockCutTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity12BlockCutTreeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BlockCutTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/BlockCutTree":{"title":"BlockCutTree","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The block–cut tree of an undirected graph (Harary’s block-cutpoint tree, JGraphT’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BlockCutpointGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"): a node per block and per articulation point, and an edge joining each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"block to each articulation point it contains. Blocks are numbered as in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blocks"},{"type":"text","text":", articulation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"points by their place in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"articulationPoints"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order). It is a forest: one tree per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected component with an edge that is not a self-loop; isolated vertices are no node."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/blockcuttree","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BlockCutTree"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BlockCutTree"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/BlockCutTree"},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/IncidenceGraphView":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","url":"\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"IncidenceGraphView","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}]}}}